{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The 2025 US population is 341,784,857.\n\nNow I need to create a metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents. I'll create a build script that joins these two pieces of information and calculates the rate. The key here is that it's a whole-table total from farmers_markets divided by a single row from census_population.\n\nFollowing the skill's guidance for \"No shared key — a whole-table total against a single reference row\" pattern, I'll create a script that:\n1. Reads both sources\n2. Creates an aggregate of farmers markets (sum, excluding territories)\n3. Gets the US population 2025\n4. Joins on a constant key\n5. Calculates the metric","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a build script that joins both datasets and calculates the farmers markets per 100,000 residents:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Lg8Sd7Y81ARM74949BMNPd","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets excluding territories\ntotals = fact.filter(~fact.state_name.isin(['Puerto Rico', 'Virgin Islands'])).aggregate(\n    total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum()\n).mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n\n# Get US 2025 population\ndenom = (ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\")\n         .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n         .mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    totals.join(denom, totals.k == denom.k)\n    .mutate(farmers_markets_per_100k=totals.total_farmers_markets / denom.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"farmers_markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":764,"cacheRead":17842,"cacheWrite":234,"totalTokens":18852,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0038200000000000005,"cacheRead":0.0017842000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.0002925,"total":0.0059087},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":171},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786913026755,"responseId":"msg_011Ce75X7qz5bQVRtPYmA1D3","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Lg8Sd7Y81ARM74949BMNPd","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1300 bytes to .xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786913034980}]}
